        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T13:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not define this as a single bit, like you would normally expect for a flag? (i.e. `BIT(0)`). You can still pass a `u64 flags` through the priv pointer.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "88b473c6f95b64f12c1b2e6ef1cc17738e52ad36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7951502b_5dd20c53",
        "filename": "kernel/dma/swiotlb.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T16:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I was concerned that I\u0027d need to reason about the alignment of the pointer. But that should be ok as we never keep the flag around (the pointer is allocated with kzalloc() which should be aligned)",
      "parentUuid": "6663500b_0415b3cd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "88b473c6f95b64f12c1b2e6ef1cc17738e52ad36",
