    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b22695ec_c24bfc6c",
        "filename": "kernel/dma/swiotlb.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1860,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T13:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we call `set_memory_encrypted()` for the encryption case, rather than rely on the default state of memory being encrypted? I don\u0027t think it matters with pKVM, but you can imagine other hypervisors that explicitly allocate the reserved memory regions (i.e. specify the base address in DT) and may have a pre-shared (decrypted) window.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1860,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1860,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "88b473c6f95b64f12c1b2e6ef1cc17738e52ad36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "697c5322_1e5eef99",
        "filename": "kernel/dma/swiotlb.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1860,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T16:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not aware of such cases. But, I\u0027d rather keep the default behavior as is as that would be a big shift from upstream and we know for pKVM memory is encrypted by default.",
      "parentUuid": "b22695ec_c24bfc6c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1860,
